+# Draft DPA / BYOK Clauses — For Legal Review
+
## 1. Purpose Limitation and Usage
+Vendor shall process Customer Data solely to provide the API services contemplated by this Agreement and for no other purpose. Vendor shall not use Customer Data to train, improve, fine‑tune, or otherwise modify any machine learning models (including vendor's models) unless expressly authorized in writing by Customer.
+
## 2. BYOK and Key Control
+When Customer elects to use Customer-Provided Keys (BYOK) or EKM, Vendor shall accept Customer's key material or key reference for encryption of Customer Data at rest and in transit within Vendor's systems, as documented in the vendor onboarding plan. Vendor shall not export, copy or persist Customer key material outside the key holder's control, except as necessary and agreed for the BYOK workflow. Any use of Customer keys by Vendor personnel shall require dual‑control approval and be auditable.
+
## 3. Data Retention and Deletion
+Vendor shall retain Customer Data only for the period necessary to provide the Services and for no longer than [X] days after termination unless retention is required by law. Upon Customer request, Vendor shall delete (or irreversibly anonymize) Customer Data within [Y] days and certify such deletion.
+
## 4. Subprocessors and Data Residency
+Vendor shall provide a current list of subprocessors and shall obtain Customer's prior written consent before engaging new subprocessors. Vendor shall process Customer Data only in agreed regions and shall not transfer data outside approved jurisdictions without Customer consent.
+
## 5. Audit Rights and Certification
+Vendor shall maintain certifications (SOC 2 Type II, ISO 27001) and shall permit Customer, or a mutually agreed third‑party auditor, to perform audits or assessments of Vendor controls relevant to Customer Data processing once annually, subject to reasonable confidentiality protections.
+
## 6. Incident Notification and Breach Response
+Vendor shall notify Customer without undue delay and in any event within seventy‑two (72) hours of discovering a security incident materially affecting Customer Data. Vendor shall provide incident details, remediation actions, and cooperation for root cause analysis.
+
## 7. Logging & Evidence Storage
+Vendor shall allow Customer to store and retrieve request/response logs for audit purposes, subject to data minimization and redaction obligations. If Customer cannot store full logs, Vendor shall provide a mechanism to export or purge data on demand.
+
## 8. Remedies & Termination
+If Vendor materially breaches the non‑training clause or other DPA terms, Customer may (i) require immediate cessation of the offending processing, (ii) require deletion of improperly used data, and (iii) terminate the Agreement for cause.
+
